/-!
# Global generation of ample twists (Serre's Theorem A)

Let `L` be an ample line bundle on a scheme `X`. Then `X` is automatically quasi-separated
(`TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry.LineBundleClass.IsAmple.quasiSeparatedSpace`), because the affine
nonvanishing loci of global sections of a common positive tensor power cover `X` and meet in
affine basic opens of one another.

For every quasi-coherent `𝒪_X`-module `F` of finite type, all sufficiently high twists
`F ⊗ L^{⊗n}` are generated by finitely many global sections
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.exists_generatingSections_tensorPow_of_isAmple`). In
particular, for any line bundle `K`, every sufficiently high twist `K ⊗ L^{⊗n}` and every
sufficiently high power `L^{⊗n}` are globally generated
(`TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry.InvertibleSheaf.exists_isGloballyGenerated_tensorProduct_tensorPow`,
`TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry.InvertibleSheaf.exists_isGloballyGenerated_tensorPow`). No Noetherian
hypothesis is needed.

The proof first treats the case where `X` is covered by finitely many affine nonvanishing loci
`X_{sᵢ}` of global sections `sᵢ` of `L`
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.exists_generatingSections_tensorPow_of_iSup_nonvanishingLocus`).
Finitely many generators of `Γ(F, X_{sᵢ})` extend to global sections of `F ⊗ L^{⊗n}` after
tensoring with a sufficiently large power of `sᵢ`
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.exists_map_eq_tmulRight_tensorPowSection`), and tensoring with
further powers of `sᵢ` moves all generators into a common twist `n ≥ n₀` whose sections over each
`X_{sᵢ}` are spanned by their images. For a general ample line bundle, raising the defining
sections of a finite affine cover to a common multiple degree `d` reduces to the first case
applied to the finitely many sheaves `F ⊗ L^{⊗r}` (`0 ≤ r < d`).

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.isInvertible_tensorPow`: monoidal tensor powers of an
  invertible sheaf are invertible;
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.nonvanishingLocus_tensorPowSection`: for `n > 0`, the
  nonvanishing locus of `sⁿ` in `L^{⊗n}` equals the nonvanishing locus of `s` in `L`;
* `TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry.LineBundleClass.IsAmple.quasiSeparatedSpace`: a scheme carrying an
  ample line bundle is quasi-separated;
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.exists_generatingSections_tensorPow_of_iSup_nonvanishingLocus`:
  finite global generation of high twists when affine nonvanishing loci of global sections of `L`
  cover `X`;
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.exists_generatingSections_tensorPow_of_isAmple`: Serre's
  Theorem A for an ample line bundle and any quasi-coherent sheaf of finite type;
* `TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry.InvertibleSheaf.exists_isGloballyGenerated_tensorProduct_tensorPow`
  and `TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry.InvertibleSheaf.exists_isGloballyGenerated_tensorPow`: global
  generation of `K ⊗ L^{⊗n}` and `L^{⊗n}` for `n ≫ 0`.

## References

* R. Hartshorne, *Algebraic Geometry*, GTM 52, Springer, 1977, Theorem II.5.17.
* [The Stacks Project, Tags 01PR and 01Q3](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01Q3).
-/

public section

